#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subject (`agent` / `user`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:49
msgid ""
"Identity is **`type`** plus `agent_config` or `user_config` primary "
"component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:49
msgid ""
"Subjects are **not** scoped by `world_id` in a membership sense; row "
"`world_id` stays at bootstrap root (`ENTITY_ROOT_WORLD_ID`) as a table "
"placeholder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:49
msgid ""
"**`agent_config` / `user_config` body**: `default_private_world_id` — the "
"subject's single default private world (auto-created on subject create; "
"configurable from private worlds owned by the subject)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:49
msgid ""
"**Notifications** use subject entity ids as `recipient_id` (see "
"[`notifications.md`](notifications.md) and `config.yaml` "
"`notifications.user_subject_id` / `agent_subject_id`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "World namespace"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:58
msgid ""
"**`type: world`** entities are logical containers (permission/list boundary)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:58
msgid "Visibility and owner live in **`world_config` body**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:58
msgid "`private: false` — public world"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:58
msgid ""
"`private: true` + `owner_subject_id` — private world owned by an `agent` or "
"`user` entity"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:58
msgid ""
"`default_private: true` — marks the subject's **exclusive** default private "
"world (at most one per `owner_subject_id`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:58
msgid ""
"Do not confuse with semantic memory **`type=world`** (fact classification in "
"[`memory.md`](memory.md)) — that becomes `body.memory_kind=world` after "
"future migration."
msgstr ""

